rulings: ['[{\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': "Abeyance does not affect abilities which are not activated, such as static abilities and triggered abilities. It also doesn\'t stop the declaration of attackers or blockers."}, {\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': \'Abeyance never prevents mana abilities from being activated.\'}, {\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': \'Abeyance prohibits activated abilities of cards which are not on the battlefield.\'}, {\'date\': \'2008-08-01\', \'text\': "This can\'t be used as a counterspell. It will have no effect on spells which were on the stack when it was cast, nor on those cast in response to it."}]', "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Aura of Silence affects all opponents in a multiplayer game.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Because the “search” requires you to find a card with certain characteristics, you don’t have to find the card if you don’t want to.'}, {'date': '2007-07-15', 'text': 'Llanowar Sentinels can “chain”: If you put a second Llanowar Sentinel onto the battlefield as a result of this ability, that creature’s enters-the-battlefield ability triggers and allows you to search for yet another Llanowar Sentinel.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Choking Vines will make any creatures it targets become blocked, even if the creature had blocking restrictions on it. For example, you can make a creature with Islandwalk become blocked even if the defending player has Islands. This is because evasion abilities only prevent creatures from being assigned to block them.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can declare zero targets, with X=0.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Choking Vines isn’t particularly effective against creatures with trample. Since the creature with trample has no blocker to assign damage to, all the damage will be assigned to the defending player.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If a previously unblocked creature becomes blocked as a result of Choking Vines, any “When this creature becomes blocked” abilities that creature has will trigger. Any “When this creature becomes blocked by a creature” abilities that creature has won’t trigger.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'You may target a blocked creature with Choking Vines. Choking Vines will deal 1 damage to it, and have no other effect on it.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Creatures are counted on resolution.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Does not target the creatures.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The creatures are chosen on resolution, not on announcement.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Each player may use this ability as many times as they choose during their turn’s draw step.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Fire Whip is put into the graveyard if you lose control of the creature since the card text says it can only enchant a creature you control.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Remember that you tap the creature as part of the cost of activating Fire Whip’s granted ability. So, if you have two Fire Whips on a creature activating the first one will tap the creature, so you can’t use the second one or any other ability which requires tapping the creature until you find a way to untap it.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If less than seven cards in the library, move all that are there.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'If the player has fewer than 2 cards, they discard whatever they have.'}, {'date': '2013-04-15', 'text': 'Players can only respond once this spell has been cast and all its costs have been paid. No one can try to destroy the creature you sacrificed to prevent you from casting this spell.'}, {'date': '2013-04-15', 'text': 'You must sacrifice exactly one creature to cast this spell; you cannot cast it without sacrificing a creature, and you cannot sacrifice additional creatures.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Its power/toughness changes when the cumulative upkeep resolves, not when it triggers.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If you choose not to pay Mwonvuli Ooze’s cumulative upkeep, it will still get an age counter before being sacrificed. Its power and toughness will momentarily increase before being put into the graveyard, which might matter to certain other cards (such as Proper Burial).'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Nothing happens if you are instructed to remove a fuse counter from an empty card.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2004-10-04\', \'text\': \'The "sacrifice a creature" effect is not targeted. It can affect creatures with protection from black, for example.\'}, {\'date\': \'2008-04-01\', \'text\': \'The player whose turn it is chooses a creature to sacrifice, then each other player in turn order chooses a creature to sacrifice, then all chosen creatures are sacrificed at the same time.\'}]', "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The +3/+3 is also only until end of turn.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The choice of creatures is made on resolution and not on announcement.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can use mana abilities during the resolution of this spell if the player decides to pay the mana cost.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You choose whether to pay or not on resolution. If not, then you sacrifice the creature. You can choose to not pay if you control no creatures on resolution.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Although Tariff checks the converted mana cost of the creatures on the battlefield, you need to pay the creature’s actual mana cost (including color) to keep it on the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'First the active player identifies the creature they control with the highest mana cost (and chooses one if there’s a tie) and chooses whether to sacrifice it or pay mana. Then each other player in turn order does the same. All creatures sacrificed this way are sacrificed at the same time.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The coin is flipped during resolution of this spell, so you know in advance what will happen when the source deals damage the next time.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The chosen source may be a permanent, a spell on the stack, or anything referred to by something on the stack (such as a Prodigal Pyromancer that’s left the battlefield while its ability is still on the stack)'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The damage happens even if this card is not on the battlefield at the end of combat.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The discard is forced even though you choose how many to discard.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Each player chooses how many cards they would like to discard. That number may be 0.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'The value of X is recalculated constantly, so this card’s bonus varies as the number of cards in your hand varies.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'There is no penalty if it can’t attack.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'This is not a targeted ability, so it deals damage to creatures that can’t be targeted by spells and abilities.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'When combined with an effect that reads “Each creature you control can’t be blocked except by two or more creatures,” none of your creatures can be blocked.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Works even if the creature is “blocked” by an effect rather than actual creatures.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'Yes, this only affects you.'}, {'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can put creatures onto the battlefield by means other than casting them.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'A “creature spell” is any spell with the type Creature, even if it has other types such as Artifact or Enchantment. Older cards of type Summon are also Creature spells.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You can look in your library and then choose to find any number from zero to three creatures after you look at it.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You must pick a target creature, even if you are the only player with creatures on the battlefield.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You skip the next untap step that you are not skipping for any other reason. In other words, the skips save up until you skip as many as required.'}]", "[{'date': '2004-10-04', 'text': 'You still put the top creature card from your graveyard onto the battlefield even if this card is not in your graveyard when the triggered ability resolves.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If an effect or rule puts two or more cards into the same graveyard at the same time, the owner of those cards may arrange them in any order.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If you control Mistmoon Griffin when it goes to the graveyard, you exile the Griffin and return the top creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. It doesn’t matter whose graveyard the Griffin goes to.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Players may not rearrange the cards in their graveyards. This is a little-known rule because new cards that care about graveyard order haven’t been printed in years.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Say you’re the owner of both a permanent and an Aura that’s attached to it. If both the permanent and the Aura are destroyed at the same time (by Akroma’s Vengeance, for example), you decide the order they’re put into your graveyard. If just the enchanted permanent is destroyed, it’s put into your graveyard first. Then, after state-based actions are checked, the Aura (which is no longer attached to anything) is put into your graveyard on top of it.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The last thing that happens to a resolving instant or sorcery spell is that it’s put into its owner’s graveyard. —Example: You cast Wrath of God. All creatures on the battlefield are destroyed. You arrange all the cards put into your graveyard this way in any order you want. The other players in the game do the same to the cards that are put into their graveyards. Then you put Wrath of God into your graveyard, on top of the other cards.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The “top” card of your graveyard is the card that was put there most recently.'}]", "[{'date': '2005-06-01', 'text': 'Will not generally kill zero cost creatures because the age counters go on before the ability triggers. If would be possible if something like Power Conduit were removing counters.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If you don’t pay the cumulative upkeep, you’ll sacrifice Wave of Terror before your draw step begins. It won’t destroy any creatures that turn.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'This destroys creatures with converted mana cost exactly equal to the appropriate number, not equal to or less than that number.'}]", "[{'date': '2005-11-01', 'text': 'Note that the wording “Effects that alter the creature’s power alter its toughness instead, and vice versa, this turn” has been removed.'}, {'date': '2013-04-15', 'text': 'Effects that switch power and toughness apply after all other effects that change power and/or toughness, regardless of which effect was created first.'}, {'date': '2013-04-15', 'text': 'Switching a creature’s power and toughness twice (or any even number of times) effectively returns the creature to the power and toughness it had before any switches.'}]", "[{'date': '2005-11-01', 'text': 'Now becomes an artifact in addition to its other types.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If Thran Forge’s ability is activated targeting a nonartifact creature, then it’s activated again in response targeting the same creature, the second instance will resolve. The first instance will then be countered for having an illegal target, since the target is no longer a nonartifact creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2006-10-15', 'text': 'It does not target the cards, but it targets the opponent. If you can’t target an opponent, you can’t activate this ability.'}, {'date': '2007-05-01', 'text': 'After the opponent chooses which card to put into your graveyard, you draw two cards regardless of how many were actually revealed or how many you have left in your library.'}]", "[{'date': '2007-05-01', 'text': 'It targets a creature card in the graveyard. This target is selected when putting the triggered ability on the stack. The wording specifies it has to be a card other than the Hierophant.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If Sylvan Hierophant is removed from the graveyard before the ability resolves, you still return the targeted creature card from your graveyard to your hand.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If you control Sylvan Hierophant when it goes to the graveyard, you exile the Hierophant and return a creature card from your graveyard to your hand. It doesn’t matter whose graveyard the Hierophant goes to.'}]", "[{'date': '2007-05-01', 'text': 'This doesn’t trigger until the end of combat.'}]", "[{'date': '2007-05-01', 'text': 'This will always be shuffled into its owner’s library.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'A permanent that’s both a land and a creature may be chosen as both of this ability’s targets.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Both a creature and a land must be targeted when the ability triggers. If there aren’t enough legal targets, the ability doesn’t go on the stack and Goblin Grenadiers can’t be sacrificed this way.'}, {'date': '2013-04-15', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when something “attacks and isn’t blocked” triggers in the declare blockers step after blockers are declared if (1) that creature is attacking and (2) no creatures are declared to block it. It will trigger even if that creature was put onto the battlefield attacking rather than having been declared as an attacker in the declare attackers step.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'A permanent that’s more than one of these types (such as an artifact creature) counts only once.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'A “creature spell” is any spell with the type Creature, even if it has other types such as Artifact or Enchantment. Older cards of type Summon are also Creature spells.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Activating the activated ability will prevent Ertai’s Familiar from phasing out for any reason, not just due to its own phasing ability.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Casting Debt of Loyalty puts a regeneration shield on a creature. If, later in the turn, that creature would be destroyed, instead it regenerates and you gain control of it. Note that it will be tapped when you gain control of it. The control change has no duration; you’ll retain control of that creature until the game ends or until some other effect causes it to change control.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If a creature has two regeneration shields on it — one from a Debt of Loyalty you cast and one from another effect — and it would be destroyed, its controller chooses which regeneration shield to use. If that player chooses to use the Debt of Loyalty shield, you’ll gain control of the creature. If the player chooses to use the other shield, you won’t gain control of the creature, but the Debt of Loyalty shield will remain on that creature for the rest of the turn (in case it would be destroyed again).'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If you cast Debt of Loyalty but nothing happens to the targeted creature for the rest of the turn that would cause it to be destroyed, Debt of Loyalty has no visible effect. The regeneration shield wears off at the end of the turn. If the creature regenerates during a later turn, you won’t gain control of it.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'You may cast Debt of Loyalty targeting a creature you already control. If you do, and that creature would be destroyed later in the turn, it will regenerate and you’ll gain control of it (though gaining control of a creature you already control usually has no visible effect).'}, {'date': '2013-07-01', 'text': 'A creature with indestructible never needs to regenerate, so Debt of Loyalty will have no effect on it.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Circling Vultures’s discard ability is a static ability, not an activated ability. Although it acts like an activated ability that says “Discard Circling Vultures: Nothing happens,” it is not one and cards like Pithing Needle or Abeyance won’t prevent you from being able to discard it.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If an effect or rule puts two or more cards into the same graveyard at the same time, the owner of those cards may arrange them in any order.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If the creature is no longer on the battlefield when the ability resolves, you may still perform the action if you want.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Players may not rearrange the cards in their graveyards. This is a little-known rule because new cards that care about graveyard order haven’t been printed in years.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Say you’re the owner of both a permanent and an Aura that’s attached to it. If both the permanent and the Aura are destroyed at the same time (by Akroma’s Vengeance, for example), you decide the order they’re put into your graveyard. If just the enchanted permanent is destroyed, it’s put into your graveyard first. Then, after state-based actions are checked, the Aura (which is no longer attached to anything) is put into your graveyard on top of it.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The last thing that happens to a resolving instant or sorcery spell is that it’s put into its owner’s graveyard. —Example: You cast Wrath of God. All creatures on the battlefield are destroyed. You arrange all the cards put into your graveyard this way in any order you want. The other players in the game do the same to the cards that are put into their graveyards. Then you put Wrath of God into your graveyard, on top of the other cards.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The “top” card of your graveyard is the card that was put there most recently.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'When the ability resolves, you choose whether to sacrifice the creature or perform the other action. If you can’t perform the other action, then you must sacrifice the creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Fatal Blow can’t target a creature that hasn’t been dealt damage this turn.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Fatal Blow cares whether the creature had been dealt damage during the turn, not whether there is still damage on it. If the creature had regenerated, causing all damage to clear, Fatal Blow can still target and destroy it.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'For example, if you discard four cards, you must target four different creatures and/or players. Firestorm will deal 4 damage to each of them.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The same permanent or player can’t be targeted more than once.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The value of X can’t exceed the number of cards in your hand or the number of available legal targets, whichever is smaller. X can be 0.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Giving a creature flanking after blockers have been declared won’t have any effect. Specifically: — If you give flanking to an attacking creature after blockers have been declared, it’s too late for flanking to trigger. — If you give flanking to a creature that’s blocking an attacking creature with flanking, it’s too late to prevent the blocking creature from getting -1/-1, even if the attacker’s flanking ability hasn’t resolved yet.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If Barishi isn’t in your graveyard by the time the ability resolves, you still shuffle all creature cards from your graveyard into your library.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The player who controlled Barishi when it left the battlefield is the player who controls the ability. It doesn’t matter whose graveyard Barishi is put into.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If Serrated Biskelion leaves the battlefield before its ability resolves, you’ll still put a -1/-1 counter on the targeted creature. If the target leaves the battlefield or otherwise becomes an illegal target before the ability resolves, the ability doesn’t resolve and you won’t put a -1/-1 counter on Serrated Biskelion.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If an effect or rule puts two or more cards into the same graveyard at the same time, the owner of those cards may arrange them in any order.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If the creature is no longer on the battlefield when the ability resolves, you may still perform the action if you want.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Players may not rearrange the cards in their graveyards. This is a little-known rule because new cards that care about graveyard order haven’t been printed in years.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Say you’re the owner of both a permanent and an Aura that’s attached to it. If both the permanent and the Aura are destroyed at the same time (by Akroma’s Vengeance, for example), you decide the order they’re put into your graveyard. If just the enchanted permanent is destroyed, it’s put into your graveyard first. Then, after state-based actions are checked, the Aura (which is no longer attached to anything) is put into your graveyard on top of it.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The last thing that happens to a resolving instant or sorcery spell is that it’s put into its owner’s graveyard. —Example: You cast Wrath of God. All creatures on the battlefield are destroyed. You arrange all the cards put into your graveyard this way in any order you want. The other players in the game do the same to the cards that are put into their graveyards. Then you put Wrath of God into your graveyard, on top of the other cards.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The “top” card of your graveyard is the card that was put there most recently.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'When the ability resolves, you choose whether to sacrifice the creature or perform the other action. If you can’t perform the other action, then you must sacrifice the creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If an effect or rule puts two or more cards into the same graveyard at the same time, the owner of those cards may arrange them in any order.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Players may not rearrange the cards in their graveyards. This is a little-known rule because new cards that care about graveyard order haven’t been printed in years.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Say you’re the owner of both a permanent and an Aura that’s attached to it. If both the permanent and the Aura are destroyed at the same time (by Akroma’s Vengeance, for example), you decide the order they’re put into your graveyard. If just the enchanted permanent is destroyed, it’s put into your graveyard first. Then, after state-based actions are checked, the Aura (which is no longer attached to anything) is put into your graveyard on top of it.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The last thing that happens to a resolving instant or sorcery spell is that it’s put into its owner’s graveyard. —Example: You cast Wrath of God. All creatures on the battlefield are destroyed. You arrange all the cards put into your graveyard this way in any order you want. The other players in the game do the same to the cards that are put into their graveyards. Then you put Wrath of God into your graveyard, on top of the other cards.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The “top” card of your graveyard is the card that was put there most recently.'}, {'date': '2013-04-15', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when something “attacks and isn’t blocked” triggers in the declare blockers step after blockers are declared if (1) that creature is attacking and (2) no creatures are declared to block it. It will trigger even if that creature was put onto the battlefield attacking rather than having been declared as an attacker in the declare attackers step.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If an effect or rule puts two or more cards into the same graveyard at the same time, the owner of those cards may arrange them in any order.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Players may not rearrange the cards in their graveyards. This is a little-known rule because new cards that care about graveyard order haven’t been printed in years.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Say you’re the owner of both a permanent and an Aura that’s attached to it. If both the permanent and the Aura are destroyed at the same time (by Akroma’s Vengeance, for example), you decide the order they’re put into your graveyard. If just the enchanted permanent is destroyed, it’s put into your graveyard first. Then, after state-based actions are checked, the Aura (which is no longer attached to anything) is put into your graveyard on top of it.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The last thing that happens to a resolving instant or sorcery spell is that it’s put into its owner’s graveyard. —Example: You cast Wrath of God. All creatures on the battlefield are destroyed. You arrange all the cards put into your graveyard this way in any order you want. The other players in the game do the same to the cards that are put into their graveyards. Then you put Wrath of God into your graveyard, on top of the other cards.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The “top” card of your graveyard is the card that was put there most recently.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If the creature is no longer on the battlefield when the ability resolves, you may still perform the action if you want.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Peacekeeper’s ability doesn’t cause the combat phase or the declare attackers step to be skipped.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'When the ability resolves, you choose whether to sacrifice the creature or perform the other action. If you can’t perform the other action, then you must sacrifice the creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If the creature is no longer on the battlefield when the ability resolves, you may still perform the action if you want.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'When the ability resolves, you choose whether to sacrifice the creature or perform the other action. If you can’t perform the other action, then you must sacrifice the creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If the defending player controls no artifacts that you can target, the ability doesn’t go on the stack and you can’t pay {R}.'}, {'date': '2013-04-15', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when something “attacks and isn’t blocked” triggers in the declare blockers step after blockers are declared if (1) that creature is attacking and (2) no creatures are declared to block it. It will trigger even if that creature was put onto the battlefield attacking rather than having been declared as an attacker in the declare attackers step.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If the first ability is activated and resolves, then the second ability is activated and resolves, Chimeric Sphere will be a 3/2 creature. It won’t have flying.'}, {'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If you choose not to pay Revered Unicorn’s cumulative upkeep, it will still get an age counter before being sacrificed, which impacts the amount of life you gain.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Revered Unicorn’s leaves-the-battlefield ability triggers no matter how it leaves the battlefield, not just when you don’t pay its cumulative upkeep.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If you control Betrothed of Fire, but it’s attached to a creature you don’t control, no one can activate the last ability. The creature’s controller can’t activate it because that player doesn’t control the Aura. You can’t activate it because you can’t pay the cost — you can’t sacrifice a creature you don’t control.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If you don’t sacrifice the lands, Lotus Vale never enters the battlefield — it goes directly to your graveyard.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'If you don’t sacrifice the lands, Scorched Ruins never enters the battlefield — it goes directly to your graveyard.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'In other words, if you sacrifice Heart of Bogardan rather than pay its cumulative upkeep, X is equal to the amount of mana last spent to pay its cumulative upkeep.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Lava Storm may be cast at any time, but it will have no effect unless there are attacking or blocking creatures on the battlefield (which exist only during certain steps of the combat phase).'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Llanowar Druid’s ability untaps all Forests on the battlefield, not just the ones you control.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Odylic Wraith’s ability triggers when it deals any kind of damage to a player, not just when it deals combat damage.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Psychic Vortex’s cumulative upkeep ability has you draw cards as a cost. If you choose to do so, and some or all of those draws are replaced by replacement effects, you are still considered to have paid the cumulative upkeep cost.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'You may choose to draw cards to pay the cumulative upkeep cost even if the number of cards you’d have to draw exceeds the number of cards in your library. If enough of those draws are replaced by replacement effects so you don’t actually attempt to draw a card with an empty library, everything’s fine. However, if you do attempt to draw a card with an empty library this way, Psychic Vortex will remain on the battlefield but you’ll lose the game as a state-based action as soon as the cumulative upkeep ability finishes resolving.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Serenity’s triggered ability destroys itself too.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Since the activated ability doesn’t have a tap symbol in its cost, you can tap a creature (including Llanowar Behemoth itself) that hasn’t been under your control since your most recent turn began to pay the cost.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The ability isn’t limited to creature cards in your hand. If an effect allows you to cast creature cards from some other zone, then Winding Canyons will allow you to do so as though they had flash.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The control change has no duration; you’ll retain control of that creature until the game ends or until some other effect causes it to change control. It doesn’t matter if Tolarian Entrancer leaves the battlefield, or if Tolarian Entrancer has already left the battlefield by the time the “at end of combat” ability triggers.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The lands that are tapped by Mana Web’s ability don’t produce mana as a result.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The opponent can tap their lands for mana in response to Mana Web’s ability triggering.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'When a land an opponent controls is tapped for mana, this card checks which types of mana (white, blue, black, red, green, or colorless) that land could produce using any of its mana abilities, not merely the one the player just used. Then it checks which lands that player controls have abilities that could produce any of those types of mana. Then it taps those lands.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The player may discard a card at random whether the enchanted creature is tapped or not.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The player whose turn it is pays any amount of mana they want, then each other player in turn order does the same, then all the Squirrel tokens are put onto the battlefield at the same time.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The player whose turn it is searches their library (or chooses not to), then each other player in turn order does the same. Then the player whose turn it is shuffles their library (if that player searched), then each other player in turn order does the same.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'The “at end of combat” ability triggers after combat damage resolves. Creatures dealt lethal damage in combat won’t be saved this way.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'This ability checks whether the player controls any nonblack, nonland permanents twice: once when it would trigger, and once when it resolves. If all the player’s nonland permanents are black at the time the ability would trigger, it doesn’t trigger at all. If all the player’s nonland permanents are black at the time the ability would resolve, it’s countered.'}, {'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'Urborg Stalker’s ability will trigger at the beginning of your upkeep as well.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'This covers only artifacts that are on the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2013-07-01', 'text': 'This effect applies to all activated abilities of artifacts, including mana abilities.'}, {'date': '2013-07-01', 'text': 'This effect does not prevent triggered abilities from triggering and it doesn’t stop the effects of static abilities.'}, {'date': '2016-06-08', 'text': 'Activated abilities contain a colon. They’re generally written “[Cost]: [Effect].” Some keywords are activated abilities and will have colons in their reminder text.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'When you cast Briar Shield’s activated ability, Briar Shield is put into the graveyard as a cost. The +1/+1 effect immediately ends, but the +3/+3 effect won’t begin until the ability resolves. The enchanted creature gets no bonus while Briar Shield’s ability is on the stack. If its toughness is 0 during this time, it’ll be put into the graveyard.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-04-01', 'text': 'You draw a card regardless of whether the targeted spell was countered or {1} was paid.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-08-01', 'text': 'A noncreature permanent that turns into a creature can attack, and its {T} abilities can be activated, only if its controller has continuously controlled that permanent since the beginning of their most recent turn. It doesn’t matter how long the permanent has been a creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'A maximum of one nonbanding creature can join an attacking band no matter how many creatures with banding are in it.'}, {'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'Creatures in the same band must all attack the same player or planeswalker.'}, {'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'If a creature with banding attacks, it can team up with any number of other attacking creatures with banding (and up to one nonbanding creature) and attack as a unit called a “band.” The band can be blocked by any creature that could block a single creature in the band. Blocking any creature in a band blocks the entire band. If a creature with banding is blocked, the attacking player chooses how the blockers’ damage is assigned.'}, {'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'Paying cumulative upkeep is always optional. If it’s not paid, the permanent with cumulative upkeep is sacrificed. Partial payments of the total cumulative upkeep cost can’t be made. For example, if a permanent with “cumulative upkeep {1}” has three age counters on it when its cumulative upkeep ability triggers, it gets another age counter and then its controller chooses to either pay {4} or sacrifice the permanent.'}, {'date': '2009-10-01', 'text': 'If a creature in combat has banding, its controller assigns damage for creatures blocking or blocked by it. That player can ignore the damage assignment order when making this assignment.'}]", "[{'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'A maximum of one nonbanding creature can join an attacking band no matter how many creatures with banding are in it.'}, {'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'Creatures in the same band must all attack the same player or planeswalker.'}, {'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'If a creature with banding attacks, it can team up with any number of other attacking creatures with banding (and up to one nonbanding creature) and attack as a unit called a “band.” The band can be blocked by any creature that could block a single creature in the band. Blocking any creature in a band blocks the entire band. If a creature with banding is blocked, the attacking player chooses how the blockers’ damage is assigned.'}, {'date': '2009-10-01', 'text': 'If a creature in combat has banding, its controller assigns damage for creatures blocking or blocked by it. That player can ignore the damage assignment order when making this assignment.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2008-10-01\', \'text\': \'Paying cumulative upkeep is always optional. If it\\\'s not paid, the permanent with cumulative upkeep is sacrificed. Partial payments of the total cumulative upkeep cost can\\\'t be made. For example, if a permanent with "cumulative upkeep {1}" has three age counters on it when its cumulative upkeep ability triggers, it gets another age counter and then its controller chooses to either pay {4} or sacrifice the permanent.\'}]', "[{'date': '2008-10-01', 'text': 'Paying cumulative upkeep is always optional. If it’s not paid, the permanent with cumulative upkeep is sacrificed. Partial payments of the total cumulative upkeep cost can’t be made. For example, if a permanent with “cumulative upkeep {1}” has three age counters on it when its cumulative upkeep ability triggers, it gets another age counter and then its controller chooses to either pay {4} or sacrifice the permanent.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2009-10-01\', \'text\': "You can\'t sacrifice more than one permanent."}]', "[{'date': '2009-10-01', 'text': 'Abduction may be cast targeting an untapped creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2011-06-01', 'text': 'Tapping the blocker does not remove it from combat and does not stop it from dealing or receiving damage.'}]", "[{'date': '2012-07-01', 'text': 'If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won’t be removed from combat.'}]", "[{'date': '2013-04-15', 'text': 'An ability that triggers when something “attacks and isn’t blocked” triggers in the declare blockers step after blockers are declared if (1) that creature is attacking and (2) no creatures are declared to block it. It will trigger even if that creature was put onto the battlefield attacking rather than having been declared as an attacker in the declare attackers step.'}]", "[{'date': '2013-04-15', 'text': 'If a permanent has multiple instances of cumulative upkeep, each triggers separately. However, the age counters are not connected to any particular ability; each cumulative upkeep ability will count the total number of age counters on the permanent at the time that ability resolves.'}]", "[{'date': '2013-07-01', 'text': 'This card won’t be put into your graveyard until after it’s finished resolving, which means it won’t be shuffled into your library as part of its own effect.'}]", "[{'date': '2014-07-18', 'text': 'Each of the three targets must be different. If there aren’t three different legal targets available, you can’t cast the spell.'}, {'date': '2014-07-18', 'text': 'If one or two of Cone of Flame’s targets are illegal when it resolves, you can’t change how much damage will be dealt to the remaining legal targets.'}]", "[{'date': '2017-11-17', 'text': 'If the creature is an illegal target when Guided Strike tries to resolve, it won’t resolve and none of its effects will happen. You won’t draw a card.'}]", '[{\'date\': \'2018-03-16\', \'text\': \'If your graveyard and library combined contain fewer than five cards, all of those cards will wind up in your library.\'}, {\'date\': \'2018-03-16\', \'text\': "If your graveyard and library combined contain five or more cards, you must choose five cards from among them. You can\'t choose to find fewer than that."}]', "[{'date': '2018-04-27', 'text': 'If Gaea’s Blessing has no legal target cards in a graveyard, either because its targets became illegal or because you didn’t choose any, the target player shuffles their library.'}, {'date': '2018-04-27', 'text': 'If an effect puts multiple cards from your library into your graveyard at once, put all of those cards there before Gaea’s Blessing shuffles your graveyard into your library.'}]", "[{'date': '2018-12-07', 'text': 'Angelic Renewal’s ability triggers if a creature you own dies under another player’s control.'}, {'date': '2018-12-07', 'text': 'If Angelic Renewal leaves the battlefield before its triggered ability resolves, you won’t be able to sacrifice it and the creature can’t be returned to the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2018-12-07', 'text': 'If a token creature is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, you can sacrifice Angelic Renewal, but nothing will be returned to the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2018-12-07', 'text': 'If an animated permanent that’s not normally a creature is put into your graveyard from the battlefield, Angelic Renewal can return that card to the battlefield.'}, {'date': '2018-12-07', 'text': 'If multiple creatures are put into your graveyard at once, Angelic Renewal triggers multiple times, but it can only be sacrificed once and only brings back one creature.'}]", "[{'date': '2022-12-08', 'text': 'If the last mining counter is removed from Gemstone Mine in some way other than activating its ability, Gemstone Mine won’t be sacrificed (and its ability can’t be activated).'}]"]
foreign_names: ["[{'name': 'Aboroth', 'text': 'Kumulative Versorgung- Lege eine -1/-1-Marke auf Aboroth.', 'type': 'Beschwörung von Aboroth', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'd5774313-6135-42fe-9d69-828bd4d1e15b'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Aboroth', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '2da7c570-b880-43d7-b0c5-995b200304e8'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Aboroth', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '5f250c26-a33d-4a80-969e-92e95044def9'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Aboroth', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '157e8cce-4528-41b5-a37c-0f2146fcb438'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'アボロス', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '85d8f309-7275-4f3b-9b5c-b426b84fdeec'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Aboroth', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'bc11ba09-d885-4b95-9aeb-6fdaaef1da79'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Abschwörung', 'text': 'Opfere eine blaue bleibende Karte: Neutralisiere einen Zauberspruch Deiner Wahl.', 'type': 'Unterbrechungszauber', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '5d60d9ee-2c57-4ba4-ab4c-e9052bfb64b3'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Abjurar', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'ac1c5313-3fa2-4274-b2c4-e91712e87b4e'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Abjuration', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '6838b46c-f0cc-420b-83bd-87eb8b9bcc7d'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Abiura', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '82508332-ead8-4c02-99d3-5073194fd89e'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': '拒絶', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '6479cffa-369c-4a2f-84e3-158fe2fa138a'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Abjurar', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '780e1a2f-a0fa-454b-9e23-a95e3ee9dfcd'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", '[{\'name\': \'Alabasterdrache\', \'text\': \'Fliegend\\nWenn der Alabasterdrache aus dem Spiel auf dem Friedhof landet, mische den Alabasterdrachen in die Bibliothek seines Besitzers.\', \'type\': \'Beschwörung eines Drachen\', \'flavor\': None, \'language\': \'German\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'ae9f094f-cb41-42bb-b5c0-16877b58f547\'}, \'multiverseid\': None}, {\'name\': \'Dragón de alabastro\', \'flavor\': None, \'language\': \'Spanish\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'9a07ecad-d0dc-4d2f-bb04-06b44af38768\'}, \'multiverseid\': None}, {\'name\': "Dragon d\'albâtre", \'flavor\': None, \'language\': \'French\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'6d1a37e2-cee1-4463-b3b3-ca7532f08a21\'}, \'multiverseid\': None}, {\'name\': "Drago d\'Alabastro", \'flavor\': None, \'language\': \'Italian\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'8ec57c1d-f139-428a-baa5-fc467d56758a\'}, \'multiverseid\': None}, {\'name\': \'純白のドラゴン\', \'flavor\': None, \'language\': \'Japanese\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'1aef9e50-ef9e-4e2e-9c5a-c8e269d4c513\'}, \'multiverseid\': None}, {\'name\': \'Dragão de Alabastro\', \'flavor\': None, \'language\': \'Portuguese (Brazil)\', \'identifiers\': {\'scryfallId\': \'8f7eda03-c268-44c0-bc7a-69fe0138e631\'}, \'multiverseid\': None}]', "[{'name': 'Almosen', 'text': '1, entferne die oberste Karte aus Deinem Friedhof ganz aus dem Spiel: Verhindere 1 Schadenspunkt bei einer Kreatur.', 'type': 'Verzauberung', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '114295a5-d88e-46fe-9417-f6e67220e68d'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Limosna', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '1996aa5e-bf38-4800-a3cf-efd6b1425ba7'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Aumône', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'd43510ea-12e9-464a-87ec-eb6a0c42a692'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Carità', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'f258c3af-f01f-4f59-8703-496eeac1e73c'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': '喜捨', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '0854d6fd-2430-4c39-a12c-5e1c1e004e1b'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Donativo', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '3233b144-40c5-43e6-ac0c-e40efd4dae51'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Apathie', 'text': 'Die verzauberte Kreatur enttappt nicht während der Enttap-Phase ihres Beherrschers.\\nDer Beherrscher der verzauberten Kreatur kann während seiner Versorgungsphase eine zufällig bestimmte Karte aus seiner Hand abwerfen, um die Kreatur zu enttappen.', 'type': 'Verzaubere Kreatur', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '5ca4d036-488b-4a81-a946-a5851e788e18'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Apatía', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'ea9f9d06-1779-441e-8181-9ddd46ef2509'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Apathie', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '076a0830-4557-46a1-b851-3b60ecdf59e6'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Apatia', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '912700c5-b9d8-435a-9b54-2d920adebf5b'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': '無気力', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '1e107108-318d-4102-b64e-855c94b34521'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Apatia', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '47a6ac9e-7bd8-461b-9990-28fe1267eea2'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Argivische Restauration', 'text': 'Bringe eine Artefaktkarte Deiner Wahl aus Deinem Friedhof direkt ins Spiel.', 'type': 'Hexerei', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '31133bb4-e7d0-45c1-9010-76b482e7eda2'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Restauración argiviana', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '8ac18c5c-15b3-49a8-bc28-36997203db33'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Restauration argiviane', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '6516b294-345c-4899-a788-3d829276cbf4'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Riparazione Argiviana', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'e8adc7be-254d-45ef-a90f-1e569ac2383d'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'アーギヴィーアの修復術', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '2777c679-7087-4201-88ef-7990d27b0554'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Restauração Argiviana', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'c6c198ca-203c-4460-b97a-47af7a048fe5'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Argivischer Fund', 'text': 'Bringe eine Artefaktkarte oder eine Verzauberungskarte Deiner Wahl aus Deinem Friedhof zurück auf Deine Hand.', 'type': 'Spontanzauber', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'German', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'd2b5e2af-2a14-42e4-930d-0a82cdcda650'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Hallazgo argiviano', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Spanish', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '37caee3a-8890-4cd4-9ee1-24d1838aeba5'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Trouvaille argiviane', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'French', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'f9563201-d63e-4aea-854d-940fa335960e'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Reperto di Argivia', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Italian', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': '3b4fd39a-cd3c-415c-b90a-501bc06cdb57'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'アーギヴィーアの発見', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Japanese', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'eed622c4-99b2-4822-8f13-d23027ea5062'}, 'multiverseid': None}, {'name': 'Achado Argiviano', 'flavor': None, 'language': 'Portuguese (Brazil)', 'identifiers': {'scryfallId': 'd0b77dad-cbc7-4870-a71c-dbd8f745f075'}, 'multiverseid': None}]", "[{'name': 'Aschenmauer', 'text': 'Wenn die Aschenmauer block